ot be rejected\"\n                                + \" start=\" + start\n                                + \" end=\" + end\n                                + \" rawStartIndex=\" + rawStartIndex\n                                + \" rawEndIndex=\" + rawEndIndex,\n                        e);\n            }\n            throw e;\n        }\n\n        /*\n         * Contract asserted: createCopy(start,end) returns the inclusive subseries bounded by\n         * ordered, non-null periods. When no source items lie in [start,end], the copied subseries\n         * must be empty. A throw-deleting or bookkeeping-skipping patch can avoid the historical\n         * exception yet still return the wrong non-empty series, so we assert observable emptiness\n         * through the public API after the real library call.\n         */\n        assertEmptySeries(copy, \"gap-empty\", start, end);\n\n        Day innerStart = start;\n        Day innerEnd = end;\n        if (data != null && start.compareTo(end) < 0) {\n            int outerStartOffset = daysBetween(left, start);\n            int outerEndOffset = daysBetween(left, end);\n            if (outerStartOffset <= outerEndOffset) {\n                int innerStartOffset = data.consumeInt(outerStartOffset, outerEndOffset);\n                int innerEndOffset = data.consumeInt(innerStartOffset, outerEndOffset);\n                Day s = addDays(left, innerStartOffset);\n                Day e = addDays(left, innerEndOffset);\n                if (s != null && e != null) {\n                    innerStart = s;\n                    innerEnd = e;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        try {\n            TimeSeries innerCopy = series.createCopy(innerStart, innerEnd);\n            assertEmptySeries(innerCopy, \"subgap-empty\", innerStart, innerEnd);\n        } catch (RuntimeException e) {\n            if (isRootCause(e)) {\n                throw new RuntimeException(\n                        \"[oracle:subgap-accept] metamorphic